            <ArticleTitle>An unusual cause of chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>38-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pericardial cysts are rare mediastinal cysts, which are commonly asymptomatic. We report the case of a middle-aged lady, with a previous short history of chest pain, who was found to have a focal pericardial density, felt to have been a consequence of haemorrhage into such a cyst.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
